# Manual calls against a sidecar from a launch profile (F5) or from scripts/dev-sidecar.ps1.
# Run ./scripts/seed-dev-db.ps1 one time first.
#
# The transport is stateless: the 2026-07-28 protocol revision removed the Mcp-Session-Id header
# (SEP-2567) and the initialize handshake (SEP-2575). Every request below is therefore
# self-contained, and there is no session id to copy from one request to the next.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = dev-token

### Process health. It needs no token and it touches no database.
GET {{host}}/health

### No Authorization header. Expect 401 with a bare "Bearer" challenge.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}

### A wrong token. Expect the same 401: the answer does not state which check failed.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer not-the-token
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}

### The tool list. It holds the permitted tools only.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}

### The schema tool. It returns DDL text and no row data.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"schema","arguments":{}}}

### The query tool. Rows come back as TOON, with the truncated flag.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"sql":"SELECT id, status, retry FROM jobs ORDER BY id"}}}

### A hard boundary. Expect isError with "QueryRejected", and no filesystem path in the text.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"sql":"ATTACH DATABASE '/tmp/x.db' AS x"}}}

### Two statements in one request. Expect isError with "InvalidQuery".
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"query","arguments":{"sql":"SELECT 1; DROP TABLE jobs"}}}

### A tool that the permission set does not cover. Start the sidecar with -Permissions read, then
### expect a forbidden answer although the name is correct.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"schema","arguments":{}}}

### The initialize handshake. A client on the 2025-11-25 revision or earlier sends it. The server
### answers it, and the tool requests above work without it.
POST {{host}}/db/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-11-25","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"mcp.http","version":"1.0"}}}
